WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:05.005
- I think it's been remarkable
to have this level of panic.

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.441
You know, Governor Newsom,

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:10.410 align:start size:84% position:16%
for example, closed
the zoos again.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.048
Now, if you're gonna lock up
every poor child in Los Angeles

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:17.417
or San Diego or San Francisco,

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:21.688 align:start size:97% position:3%
so that they're in a little
apartment, they have no space.

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:24.924 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then you're gonna
close all the public parks.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:27.460
What are these little
kids supposed to do?

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.962
And it strikes me

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:33.299
that what you end up with is
a public health dictatorship,

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:37.137
which is very singular in
how it measures things.

00:00:37.137 --> 00:00:40.507 align:start size:97% position:3%
I had a university president
say to me the other day

00:00:40.507 --> 00:00:44.310
that he will lose more
young people to suicide

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.914
and drunk driving than
he will lose to COVID.

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:51.584 align:start size:84% position:16%
And he said,
"They're reopening."

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:53.486
He cannot understand

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:55.889
why people have any doubt
at all about reopening.

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:58.458
(upbeat music)

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:06.966 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
- I'm Dave Rubin and this
is "The Rubin Report"

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:09.402 align:start position:0% line:0%
reminder everybody to subscribe
to our YouTube channel

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:12.172 line:0%
and click that pesky
notification bell.

00:01:12.172 --> 00:01:15.141
And joining me today is the
former Speaker of the House,

00:01:15.141 --> 00:01:17.243
the author of over 40 books

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:20.580 align:start size:88% position:13%
and the chairman of
Gingrich 360 Consulting,

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.615
Newt Gingrich, welcome
to The Rubin Report.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.084
- Well, it's good
to be with you.

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:25.585
So exciting.

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:26.820
- I'm glad to have you.

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.255
You are in Rome at the moment.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.991
What's going on in
Rome these days.

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:33.493 line:0%
- Well, as you know,

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:36.596 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
my wife Callista is the
Ambassador to the Vatican,

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:38.531 line:0%
so that's why we're here.

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.400 align:start size:84% position:16%
Rome actually has
had a huge comeback.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:45.105
They got in a big trouble
back in February because

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:50.076 align:start position:0%
there are about 100,000 Chinese
workers in Northern Italy,

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:55.115
and they were allowing
the flights to continue.

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:58.118
So they were literally
flying in from Wuhan

00:01:58.118 --> 00:02:00.019
bringing the disease right here.

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:03.223
And it got so out of control
that their hospital system

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:06.392 align:start position:0%
was breaking down and they
were starting to triage people.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.428 align:start size:88% position:13%
And if you were over
80, they basically said,

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:11.998 line:0%
"You're not getting, we're
not gonna take care of you."

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:15.735 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
He in fact, Callista
helped Samaritan's Purse

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:18.505 line:0%
Franklin Graham's operation.

00:02:18.505 --> 00:02:20.807 line:0%
They flew in an entire hospital,

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:23.443
68 beds, 60 doctors and nurses

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:25.945 align:start size:88% position:13%
into the worst hit
part of Northern Italy.

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:28.848
So the Italian Government
closed everything down.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:32.852
We had grocery stores,
pharmacies, gas stations.

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.456
That's it.

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:39.392
If you were in the street,

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:42.829 align:start size:84% position:16%
you had to have a good
excuse in writing,

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:45.231
or you could be fined $3,200.

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:50.103 align:start size:88% position:13%
So for 10 weeks,
Callista ran the embassy

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:52.138
from our house virtually,

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:56.476
and we do amazing amount
of Zoom and go to meeting.

00:02:56.476 --> 00:03:00.046
And what have you,
and for 10 weeks,

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:02.048
they basically starved the virus

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:04.083
and gradually got
it under control.

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:06.586 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's now sufficiently
under control

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:10.356
that they've reopened the
restaurants, the museums,

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:12.091
public parks, stores,

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.729
and you see people
walking around now,

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:21.634 align:start size:88% position:13%
problem readily is about
14% of their economy.

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:26.639
$137 is tourism, and they
don't have any tourism yet.

00:03:27.507 --> 00:03:29.642
So places like the Colosseum,

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:32.579 align:start size:84% position:16%
the last year got
23,000 people a day.

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:35.748 align:start size:88% position:13%
You know, they maybe
have 500 or 1,000 a day.

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:38.351 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's a real economic
crisis for them.

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:40.753
But in terms of the pandemic,

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:46.226 align:start position:0%
they are in dramatically,
dramatically better shape today.

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:47.660
- Yeah.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:49.128 align:start size:97% position:3%
So we're holding this
interview for a couple days.

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:51.497
So I don't wanna ask you
anything about specifically

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:54.767
what's happening today,
but generally speaking

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:58.304 align:start size:88% position:13%
the way you see the
lockdown now in America,

00:03:58.304 --> 00:04:01.641
and I'm here in Los Angeles
and literally just yesterday,

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:03.943
Newsom put us in
another lockdown

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:07.247
and that these things seem to
keep continually happening.

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:09.182
We're watching some spikes,

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:13.286 align:start position:0%
it just seems that no one knows
who to trust at the moment.

00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:16.656
What's your take about how
the states have done it,

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:18.725
where Trump fits into this.

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:20.660
And is there something that you,

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:23.196 align:start size:84% position:16%
would have been
doing differently as
Speaker of the House

00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:27.200
to push your guys, to push
certain things differently?

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:30.203 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Well, I think
it's been remarkable

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:34.574
to have this level of panic.

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:36.242
You know, Governor Newsom,

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:38.411
for example, closed
the zoo's again.

00:04:38.411 --> 00:04:42.949
Now, if you're gonna lock up
every poor child in Los Angeles

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:45.318
or San Diego or San Francisco,

00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:49.622 align:start size:97% position:3%
so that they're in a little
apartment, they have no space.

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:53.059 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then you're gonna
close all the public parks.

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:55.361
What are these little
kids supposed to do?

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:58.031
And it strikes me that
what you end up with

00:04:58.031 --> 00:05:01.167
is a public health dictatorship,

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:04.637
which is very singular in
how it measures things.

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:08.308 align:start size:97% position:3%
I had a university president
say to me the other day

00:05:08.308 --> 00:05:12.078
that he will lose more
young people to suicide

00:05:12.078 --> 00:05:15.648
and drunk driving than
he will lose to COVID.

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:18.384 align:start size:84% position:16%
And he said,
"They're reopening."

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:21.254
He cannot understand

00:05:21.254 --> 00:05:24.023
why people have any doubt
at all about reopening.

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:25.925
And so I would start from there.

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:29.762
The people you need to worry
about, half of all the deaths,

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:33.399 align:start position:0%
are people who are over 70
years of age and in particular,

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:36.235
he go the more you go up at
80 years of more dangerous

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:38.171
at 90 it's even more dangerous.

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:42.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you know that you wanna
really work to protect

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:43.643
people who are over 70.

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:46.245 align:start size:97% position:3%
But you don't need to really
work to protect people

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:47.347
who are 13.

00:05:48.314 --> 00:05:49.916
And the idea that we're,

00:05:49.916 --> 00:05:51.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
we've gone from a
country that used to know

00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:53.453
how to open one house,

00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:56.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
school rooms and have
seven classes in one room

00:05:56.723 --> 00:05:58.725
and people actually
learn how to read

00:05:58.725 --> 00:06:03.229 align:start position:0%
to an extraordinarily expensive
union dominated bureaucracy

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:04.964
that doesn't wanna teach.

00:06:04.964 --> 00:06:06.366
And you're gonna have
this in Los Angeles,

00:06:06.366 --> 00:06:07.800
they've got it in New York.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, they have in
Fairfax County, Virginia,

00:06:10.236 --> 00:06:12.338
one of the biggest and
richest school districts

00:06:12.338 --> 00:06:16.809
in the country, why would
we pay people to not teach?

00:06:16.809 --> 00:06:19.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why would we have all
these big fancy buildings

00:06:19.078 --> 00:06:20.580
nobody can go to?

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:24.717 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think it really raises
very profound questions

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:25.885
about the whole system.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:28.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah, well that
actually is perfect segue

00:06:28.755 --> 00:06:30.256
because I was gonna say,

00:06:30.256 --> 00:06:32.425
as someone that's a true
lover of American history

00:06:32.425 --> 00:06:33.860
and has written about it,

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:35.328 align:start size:97% position:3%
and you talk about American
history all the time,

00:06:35.328 --> 00:06:38.531 align:start position:0%
are you sort of shocked the
way the average American person

00:06:38.531 --> 00:06:43.536
just sort of takes orders and
doesn't necessarily ask why

00:06:44.404 --> 00:06:45.638
are these things happening?

00:06:45.638 --> 00:06:47.540
You know, at one time it
was flatten the curve.

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:49.509
We don't hear the phrase
flatten the curve anymore.

00:06:49.509 --> 00:06:50.443
We haven't heard it.

00:06:50.443 --> 00:06:51.377
(clears throat)

00:06:51.377 --> 00:06:52.612
Excuse me for about six weeks.

00:06:52.612 --> 00:06:53.980
Now it seems to
be something else

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.715
or they just give us an order

00:06:55.715 --> 00:06:57.483 align:start size:84% position:16%
and they don't
really tell you why.

00:06:58.918 --> 00:07:01.888
- Well I mean, part of it has
been, I think the evolution

00:07:01.888 --> 00:07:06.159
from a news media to
a propaganda media,

00:07:06.159 --> 00:07:08.795 align:start size:84% position:16%
so that you have these
waves of coverage.

00:07:08.795 --> 00:07:12.064 align:start size:88% position:13%
I compared it to
watching the flagellate

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:14.267
in the middle ages,
this was a group.

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:16.903
They would go from city to
city beating themselves.

00:07:16.903 --> 00:07:21.407
And so you have all of these
people out here who they panic.

00:07:23.376 --> 00:07:25.244 align:start size:88% position:13%
The truth is if you
look at the death rate,

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:26.746
there's no reason to panic.

00:07:28.381 --> 00:07:32.485
This is not the bubonic
plague, it's not Ebola.

00:07:33.619 --> 00:07:35.188
Most people who get,

00:07:35.188 --> 00:07:37.790 align:start size:88% position:13%
first of all an amazing
percentage who get

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.762
the Chinese virus,
which is what it is.

00:07:42.762 --> 00:07:45.531 align:start size:88% position:13%
Most of them don't
even know they have it.

00:07:49.035 --> 00:07:50.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you're told
somebody tested positive,

00:07:50.937 --> 00:07:53.039
who was quote symptomatic.

00:07:53.039 --> 00:07:57.376 align:start size:97% position:3%
That means whatever symptoms
they had were so mild

00:07:57.376 --> 00:08:00.112
that it didn't affect them.

00:08:00.112 --> 00:08:02.515
So you have to then stop
and say, "Wait a second,

00:08:02.515 --> 00:08:06.352
"why are we panicking over..."

00:08:06.352 --> 00:08:07.587
You know, the numbers go up,

00:08:07.587 --> 00:08:09.989
with the numbers go up
with people under 35

00:08:09.989 --> 00:08:11.357
who are totally healthy.

00:08:12.425 --> 00:08:13.926
And I think,

00:08:13.926 --> 00:08:15.828
I have been truly appalled

00:08:15.828 --> 00:08:17.997 align:start size:84% position:16%
my younger daughter
Jackie Cushman,

00:08:17.997 --> 00:08:19.799
as a certified financial analyst

00:08:19.799 --> 00:08:22.134
and used to run a
very large budget,

00:08:22.134 --> 00:08:24.303
billion dollar plus budget.

00:08:24.303 --> 00:08:25.404 align:start size:81% position:19%
And she said to
me the other night

00:08:25.404 --> 00:08:27.573
and just she and I discussed,

00:08:27.573 --> 00:08:29.876 align:start size:84% position:16%
she said, "I have
never seen statistics

00:08:29.876 --> 00:08:32.345
"put together so badly

00:08:32.345 --> 00:08:35.515 align:start size:97% position:3%
"that it is impossible to know
what's actually happened."

00:08:35.515 --> 00:08:38.284
And she is just literally
fed up with this things,

00:08:38.284 --> 00:08:40.853 align:start size:88% position:13%
whether it's because the
government statistics

00:08:40.853 --> 00:08:44.457
are so incompetent or whether
it's because the news media

00:08:44.457 --> 00:08:45.958
is deliberately,

00:08:45.958 --> 00:08:49.128
they're going from worst case
to worst case to worst case.

00:08:49.128 --> 00:08:51.764 align:start size:84% position:16%
So they don't tell
you that, for example,

00:08:53.199 --> 00:08:56.536
Georgia has about 10% of the
fatality rate of New York.

00:08:56.536 --> 00:09:00.006
They praise Cuomo, who is the
worst governor in the country,

00:09:00.006 --> 00:09:02.608
but has been praised so
much by the news media

00:09:02.608 --> 00:09:05.578
that he now has a very high
popularity rating in New York

00:09:05.578 --> 00:09:07.079
while he killed people.

00:09:07.079 --> 00:09:09.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, at least six to
8,000 senior citizens died

00:09:09.982 --> 00:09:13.319
because of Governor Cuomo
and decisions he made.

00:09:13.319 --> 00:09:16.088
But it somehow gets
brushed over because

00:09:16.088 --> 00:09:18.424 align:start size:84% position:16%
he's liberal and
therefore it's okay.

00:09:19.825 --> 00:09:21.360
- Yeah, so let's sit with
that for a little bit,

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.663
because, I think a lot of
people think that Trump

00:09:23.663 --> 00:09:27.099 align:start size:97% position:3%
was sort of the first guy, the
first mainstream politician

00:09:27.099 --> 00:09:29.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a modern sense to
really go after the media.

00:09:29.735 --> 00:09:33.105 align:start size:97% position:3%
But I remember your campaign
in 2012 really well,

00:09:33.105 --> 00:09:35.908
and you were capturing
that populous sentiment.

00:09:35.908 --> 00:09:37.543
And during the debates,

00:09:37.543 --> 00:09:39.245
you won a couple
of debates in a row

00:09:39.245 --> 00:09:40.780
and you had the crowds cheering

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:42.915
and screaming to the point that,

00:09:42.915 --> 00:09:44.684
the networks were asking crowds,

00:09:44.684 --> 00:09:46.652
not to make sounds
during the debates,

00:09:46.652 --> 00:09:49.155 align:start size:88% position:13%
which in many ways,
deflated your candidacy

00:09:49.155 --> 00:09:52.124
because you were
using their energy.

00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:54.594
That's sort of relevant

00:09:54.594 --> 00:09:56.062
to what you just said
there about Cuomo,

00:09:56.062 --> 00:09:59.098
because Democrats seem
to be able to get away

00:09:59.098 --> 00:10:00.399
with virtually anything

00:10:00.399 --> 00:10:01.867
and then blaming it
on the other guy,

00:10:01.867 --> 00:10:05.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
because they know the
media runs cover for them.

00:10:05.204 --> 00:10:07.873
You guys don't get that luxury.

00:10:07.873 --> 00:10:08.708
(Newt laughs)

00:10:08.708 --> 00:10:10.176
- Well, look,

00:10:10.176 --> 00:10:13.779 align:start position:0%
I mean, you could tell that
the Romney was the media choice

00:10:13.779 --> 00:10:16.115
because they rigged
towards the end.

00:10:16.115 --> 00:10:18.050
They just rigged the debates.

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:20.920 line:0%
I mean, it was amazing when I
got up on stage and they said,

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:21.988 line:0%
"Nobody gets to applaud.

00:10:21.988 --> 00:10:22.955 line:0%
"Nobody has to do this.

00:10:22.955 --> 00:10:24.857 line:0%
"Nobody has to do that."

00:10:24.857 --> 00:10:29.328 line:0%
And I looked at it and he
was truly anti-popular.

00:10:29.328 --> 00:10:33.566
I mean, it was as elitist
as you could possibly be.

00:10:33.566 --> 00:10:34.667
And I frankly watched--

00:10:34.667 --> 00:10:37.303
- When you say they,

00:10:37.303 --> 00:10:38.971 align:start size:88% position:13%
do you mean that's
coming from the networks

00:10:38.971 --> 00:10:41.273
or coming from the RNC?

00:10:41.273 --> 00:10:43.409
- No, no, coming
from the network.

00:10:43.409 --> 00:10:44.977
- From the network, okay.

00:10:44.977 --> 00:10:48.214
- The network had said decided
that Romney was the low risk,

00:10:48.214 --> 00:10:52.485
moderate candidate that
they could survive with.

00:10:52.485 --> 00:10:55.855
And that I really was their
mortal enemy, which is true.

00:10:55.855 --> 00:10:59.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, if you're gonna
destroy the New York Times

00:10:59.492 --> 00:11:01.627
and turn it into a
propaganda machine,

00:11:01.627 --> 00:11:02.895
then as somebody who grew up

00:11:02.895 --> 00:11:04.630
when there really
was a news media,

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:06.265
I am deeply opposed to it

00:11:06.265 --> 00:11:09.201 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I don't mind going
head-to-head with
all these people.

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:12.738 align:start size:84% position:16%
I really admire
Trump in that sense,

00:11:12.738 --> 00:11:15.107
because I thought in 15 and 16,

00:11:15.107 --> 00:11:17.109 align:start size:84% position:16%
he did the best
job I've ever seen.

00:11:17.109 --> 00:11:18.611
I mean better than Reagan,

00:11:18.611 --> 00:11:21.414
better than me at taking
