00:28:02.947 --> 00:28:05.817
And it was really
interesting story

00:28:05.817 --> 00:28:08.653
because he went around the
country as a spokesperson.

00:28:08.653 --> 00:28:12.857
He talked gave about 375
speeches to factories.

00:28:12.857 --> 00:28:15.660 align:start position:0%
So he had a lot of practice
talking to blue collar workers,

00:28:15.660 --> 00:28:18.129
taking questions,
being a celebrity,

00:28:19.564 --> 00:28:22.267
which was great preparation
for running for governor.

00:28:22.267 --> 00:28:23.802
And in the process,

00:28:23.802 --> 00:28:25.870
Reagan was in a period where
he wouldn't fly an airplane.

00:28:25.870 --> 00:28:29.774 align:start size:97% position:3%
He did a really bouncy
flight in, I think late 45.

00:28:29.774 --> 00:28:33.311 align:start size:88% position:13%
So he did not fly an
airplane again til 1965.

00:28:33.311 --> 00:28:35.380 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so he went
everywhere by train.

00:28:35.380 --> 00:28:36.514
And the guy he worked for

00:28:36.514 --> 00:28:39.818 align:start size:88% position:13%
was a very conservative
intellectual,

00:28:39.818 --> 00:28:42.387
the head of human relations

00:28:42.387 --> 00:28:44.923
and union relations
of General Electric.

00:28:44.923 --> 00:28:46.291
And so this guy

00:28:46.291 --> 00:28:48.026 align:start size:97% position:3%
would give Reagan
conservative economic books.

00:28:48.026 --> 00:28:50.195
So here you have Reagan driving,

00:28:50.195 --> 00:28:52.263
riding across the
country in a train,

00:28:52.263 --> 00:28:55.433 align:start position:0%
reading conservative economics,
preparing his speeches.

00:28:55.433 --> 00:28:57.769
Well, Reagan came up with
a model which he really got

00:28:57.769 --> 00:28:59.804
