in the payroll tax,

00:29:35.006 --> 00:29:36.407
because it would be
enormously helpful--

00:29:36.407 --> 00:29:37.242
- You go me.

00:29:37.242 --> 00:29:38.977
- And the self-employed.

00:29:38.977 --> 00:29:40.779
And it would be more
money in the pocket

00:29:40.779 --> 00:29:42.714
of every single
working American.

00:29:42.714 --> 00:29:45.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that would be the
kind of popular proposal,

00:29:45.784 --> 00:29:48.486
that you could then
build heat on Pelosi.

00:29:48.486 --> 00:29:50.855
Not 'cause you're in the
room negotiating with her,

00:29:50.855 --> 00:29:53.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
but because you're talking
to the whole country

00:29:53.191 --> 00:29:55.527
and the country is
telling her members,

00:29:55.527 --> 00:29:57.462
"I really want you
to vote for this."

00:29:57.462 --> 00:29:59.430
So I really think that

00:29:59.430 --> 00:30:00.865
(Newt clears throat)

00:30:00.865 --> 00:30:05.270 align:start size:97% position:3%
for example, when we finally
passed welfare reform,

00:30:06.738 --> 00:30:09.507
there was a tie, there was
a poll 92% of the country,

00:30:09.507 --> 00:30:12.076
